      "content": "<h3>Sizing a HashMap to avoid resizes</h3>",
      "codeExamples": [
        "// Capacity needed for N entries without a resize: N / 0.75, rounded up to a power of two\npublic class SizingDemo {\n    static int tableSizeFor(int cap) {                               // same idea as HashMap.tableSizeFor\n        int n = 1;\n        while (n < cap) {\n            n <<= 1;\n        }\n        return n;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        for (int expected : new int[] {5, 12, 13, 100, 1000}) {\n            int needed = (int) Math.ceil(expected / 0.75);\n            System.out.println(expected + \" entries -> ask for \" + needed + \" -> table of \" + tableSizeFor(needed) + \" buckets\");\n        }\n        System.out.println(\"new HashMap<>(10) really creates a table of \" + tableSizeFor(10));\n    }\n}\n// OUTPUT:\n// 5 entries -> ask for 7 -> table of 8 buckets\n// 12 entries -> ask for 16 -> table of 16 buckets\n// 13 entries -> ask for 18 -> table of 32 buckets\n// 100 entries -> ask for 134 -> table of 256 buckets\n// 1000 entries -> ask for 1334 -> table of 2048 buckets\n// new HashMap<>(10) really creates a table of 16"
      ]
